    "created_at": "2015-08-30T08:44:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-30T10:11:57Z",
    "body": "The token seems entirely consistent with the rest of iframe@sandbox. X is\ndisabled by default, and you can use 'allow-x' to turn it back on. _shrug_\nThe cognitive overhead for developers seems trivial, and since it is a\nbreaking change, it seems reasonable to leave a workaround for any benign\nuses we accidentally bust.\n\nThat said, I'll leave it up to the illustrious editors. I've implemented\nand shipped the token in Chrome based on those two threads, but if y'all\nwould prefer to drop it, I'm sure we can make that work. It basically means\nremoving the \"unless\" clause in the change to the parsing algorithm.\n\n(Also, if someone is writing a book, they'll likely appreciate the extra\ntoken, as it'll help them hit their target page count without\ndouble-spacing or fiddling with the margins. :)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
